  "system": {
    "slug": "aria-tloak",
    "details": {
      "level": {
        "value": 11
      },
      "publicNotes": "<p>Aria T'Loak is the self-declared ruler of Omega — the largest space station in the Terminus Systems and the galaxy's most lawless port. She has held this position for centuries through a combination of overwhelming biotic power, ruthless pragmatism, and an intelligence network that rivals any government. She doesn't negotiate from weakness. Ever.</p><p><strong>I Am Omega (aura):</strong> All enemies within 30 feet of Aria take a –1 circumstance penalty to saves against her abilities. Enemies who fail a save against one of her abilities are also Frightened 1.</p><p><strong>Biotic Shockwave (2 actions):</strong> A 30-foot line of biotic force. All creatures in the area take 4d8+10 force damage (DC 30 Reflex for half).</p><p><strong>Biotic Pull (2 actions):</strong> Up to three targets within 60 feet must succeed on a DC 30 Fortitude save or be pulled 20 feet toward Aria and become Grabbed until the end of their next turn.</p><p><strong>Omega's Resolve (reaction):</strong> When Aria is reduced to 0 HP, she may spend her reaction: she is instead reduced to 1 HP and all enemies within 30 feet take 2d10 force damage (no save). 1/encounter.</p><p><strong>Kinetic Barrier:</strong> 70 Shield HP. Recharges 20 HP per turn.</p>",
      "privateNotes": "",
      "publication": {
        "title": "Mass Effect Compendium",
        "authors": "nscarpinatodev",
        "license": "ORC",
        "remaster": true
      },
      "languages": {
        "value": [],
        "details": ""
      },
      "blurb": "Absolute ruler of Omega; centuries-old asari crime lord who enforces her will through raw biotic power."
    },
